---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const description =
  'Start Up Markets is a weekly Lightcone-style synthesis across top venture firms: what’s hot, and who to network with.';
---

<Base title="About" description={description}>
  <Header />
  <main id="content" class="wrap page">
    <p class="eyebrow">About the desk</p>
    <h1>A weekly read, not a link dump.</h1>
    <div class="prose about-prose">
      <p>
        Start Up Markets stores Peter’s <em>Bleeding-Edge Markets</em> briefs. Each Monday note is a
        Lightcone-style synthesis across top venture firms: where the frontier is heating up, which
        theses partners just put in writing, and who is worth a conversation that week.
      </p>
      <p>
        The audience is a fast scan. Know what’s hot and who to network with. Skip the deal
        encyclopedia.
      </p>
      <h2>What every brief covers</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Hot areas</li>
        <li>Thesis watch</li>
        <li>Who to network with</li>
        <li>Capital signals</li>
        <li>Cooling / crowded</li>
        <li>Sources</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The archive lists every week newest first. Tags are that week’s hot areas, so a theme can be
        followed from the index. Search runs over titles, tags, and the one-line summary.
      </p>
      <p>
        A new week is a single Markdown file in <code>content/briefs/</code>. The newest brief
        sits at the top of the archive.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
